[limitations]
cache_interventions=unknown
logical_storage_interventions=unknown
description=Component contracts are exact; the live RTC dispatch (this profile only) implements the lane Timers.AmbiqApollo4_RTC register law since E-SAP-0035: WRTC-gated CNTL/CNTU pair commits the epoch clock, RPT drives the alarm cadence, IRQ2 = Enable && Status until InterruptClear. The W +0x20 refusal that drove the E-SAP-0034 ~1.01186 s HardFault/AIRCR cycle is gone and the boot escapes the cycle: the guest wakes at second occurrences, runs past 100 M instructions in 85 s of virtual time, parks in WFI (pc 0x000e1862), and only re-enters its own AIRCR helper (pc 0x000cdf5a, lr 0xffffffed) every ~120.148 s; the remaining 120 s-cadence guest-level blocker is not RTC-derived (next census territory). 2.22/2.33/2.39 keep the inert RTC stub; window access beyond 0x210 and non-4 widths stay fail-closed refusals
